course: dictionary
lesson: 8492
title: One word, three meanings: sandy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word sandy can describe a place, a colour or a name. Look at the words around it: «a sandy beach» tells you the beach is covered with sand.
explain: «Sandy hair» is not about sand at all. It describes hair that is light yellowish-brown, like sand. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? If the clues are about the ground or a place, sandy means covered with sand or full of sand.
explain: Sandy is also a name, short for Alexander, Alexandra or Sandra. If the sentence is about a person doing something, like shouting or running, sandy is probably a name. Try the meaning in the sentence to check.
fact: Sandy means covered with sand or full of sand, as in «a sandy beach».
fact: Sandy can also describe hair that is light yellowish-brown, like sand, as in «sandy hair».
fact: Sandy is also a name, short for Alexander, Alexandra or Sandra.
fact: In science, sandy soil has big grains with big gaps, so water drains through it fast.
fact: Clay soil has tiny grains packed close together, so it holds water.
exercise: «The children ran across the sandy beach.» What does sandy mean here? | Light yellowish-brown | A girl called Sandy | Full of water | *Covered with sand
exercise: «Her sandy hair shone in the sun.» What colour is her hair? | *Light yellowish-brown, like sand | Grey and wet | Black like ink | Bright blue
exercise: Which sentence uses sandy as a name? | Her hair was sandy and light. | Sandy soil drains water quickly. | The sandy path was warm under our feet. | *Sandy shouted for her friend across the playground.
test: «Sandy soil has big grains with big gaps.» Why does water drain through it fast? | Because the grains are tiny and packed close | Because sandy soil is sticky | Because sandy soil is always wet | *Because the big gaps let it run through
test: Which meaning of sandy fits «the sandy feet left prints on the floor»? | Light yellowish-brown hair | Full of water | *Covered with sand | A person named Sandy
exam: In which phrase does sandy mean light yellowish-brown? | a sandy beach | *sandy hair | sandy feet | sandy soil
